// spec: a lambda's closure as a base class (`template<typename... Ts> struct Overload : Ts... { using Ts::operator()...; };` given lambdas, the overload-set idiom) is an error where the class is laid out, until it is supported; its deduction guide deduces the arguments (Overload<L1, L2>), and a pack of bases of classes is laid out (classes/pack_of_base_classes, 2026-11-06): the closures as bases and the call through them are what is missing
// factorio: Util.hpp's make_overload, whose one user (visitVariant, around std::visit) goes with the Variant mapping (library/variant): decided 2026-10-31 to be an error until something needs it
// error: lambda_as_base_class_is_not_supported_yet.kpp:9: error: codegen does not support the layout of Overload<
// error: >: a lambda's closure as a base class (
template<typename... Ts> struct Overload : Ts... { using Ts::operator()...; };
template<typename... Ts> Overload(Ts...) -> Overload<Ts...>;
